{
  "_about": "How each creature is drawn (the client's CreatureView): its model and scale, the clip set its animations follow (anim_set), the ground speeds its walk and run cycles were authored at (0 = play at 1x), a hover height for fliers, the boss variant's model, and the name label height. Presentation only; the server never reads it. Objects (\"object\": stone or dummy) are drawn by their own views (StoneView, DummyView): a Dark Shard's model, its glow, the height of its body and label and how tall its sky beam stands; a dummy's label height and the point its painted face turns to. A web thing (rig web_object: an egg sac, a cocoon) splits open when it dies, with the `fluid` tint (r, g, b) of what is inside it; `stretch` (x, y, z) widens or heightens a model past its uniform `scale`, `silk_alpha` draws it as see-through silk.",
